Short:        Claude Code client for the Amiga
Author:       spotUP
Uploader:     UPLOADER-ADDRESS-PLACEHOLDER (spotUP)
Type:         comm/misc
Version:      @VERSION@
Replaces:     none
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0; m68k-020
Requires:     TCP/IP stack (Roadshow, Miami, AmiTCP), util/libs/AmiSSL-v5-OS3.lha for https
Distribution: Aminet

C:Claude: a Claude Code client. It reads, searches and edits files and runs
commands with your own Anthropic API key (billed to that key), or connects to Claude Code on
another computer (C:uptelnet comes with it; with both, it asks which). It stands alone: it installs on a plain
Workbench (AmigaOS 3.0 or newer) and runs in the Shell window, in a line mode; in an UP-Term
window (comm/term/up-term.lha, optional) it gets the full-screen mode and keeps its data in
UP-Term:var.

Install: unpack, double-click Install. Uninstall removes C:Claude (and an old C:ClaudeCode) and keeps
your settings in ENVARC:Claude.

Licence: MIT (UP-Term's own code).
